{
"jm66ge": "Welcome to Numbo, the little land where math is an adventure!",
"1pdzzq8": "Behind the clouds lies a tiny land called Numbo. That is where Bobby lives, the keeper of numbers.",
"xlvkfr": "Every morning, Bobby lines up the numbers 1 to 9 on a favorite shelf. Everything is neat and cheerful!",
"1ie70a3": "Suddenly, WHOOSH! A big wind blows every number far away.",
"1cbsgro": "The numbers are hiding all over the land: in a garden, a river, a hill, a cave, an island, and a village.",
"53bjvt": "Bobby cannot count without the numbers. Will you help Bobby?",
"xad0pc": "What is your name, helper?",
"tdbk34": "Nice to meet you!",
"14tc8tj": "Hooray! One by one, all the numbers are back on Bobby's shelf.",
"rs7y69": "Thank you! You are now an official Number Keeper.",
"iw30eb": "Thanks for playing Numbo. Come back any time. Bobby and the numbers will be waiting!",
"105ktef": "Hi! I am Bobby! Let us count together. Yay!",
"1a13zzo": "Great job!",
"1c5sxvi": "Exactly right!",
"o7gu2y": "You're so smart!",
"1c4cgr1": "Yes, nailed it!",
"emhmbb": "Awesome!",
"y5w9e": "Almost! Check the steps.",
"h358fh": "That's okay. Try again next time.",
"93e6cy": "Let's learn from this one.",
"krnzzt": "Yes, you found it!",
"xed0ec": "Not quite. Try once more!",
"tmyd4t": "Put two groups together. Tap plus or minus to change them. Then press the button!",
"1avvojk": "Try once more. Try counting up. Start from the bigger number!",
"1ig37ao": "Take some away. Tap a dot to take it away.",
"hcb7hu": "Try once more. Try counting back. Or check: answer plus small number equals big number.",
"1d7hn8y": "Look at the shapes. Tap one to see its sides!",
"1uxshd2": "Try once more. Look closely. Count the sides and corners one by one.",
"bm612y": "Compare lengths and read the clock. Move the sliders!",
"1osus2a": "Try once more. Look at the picture carefully. On a clock, the short hand is the hour and the long hand is the minutes.",
"1hq1c2j": "Count the pictures in each row. Move the sliders!",
"1l9wgr9": "Try once more. Look at the chart again. Find the label, then read its number.",
"kyc3wf": "Read the story. Find the key words. Pick plus or minus.",
"m1ai1": "Try once more. Find the key words in the story. Then choose plus, minus, times or divide.",
"1kb5rgs": "Add the ones first, then the tens. If you reach 10, carry 1.",
"1r1c5yq": "Take away the ones first, then the tens. Borrow if you need to.",
"4btssv": "Multiplying is adding the same number again and again. Tap a square!",
"uoggt9": "Try once more. Think of equal groups. Add the same number again and again.",
"1j7g1lo": "Share equally. Move the sliders to share the marbles.",
"13whqaf": "Try once more. Division is the opposite of multiplication. Check it with times.",
"1ghtvpc": "A fraction is part of a whole. Cut it into equal parts and look!",
"1hpqzfv": "Try once more. Look at the picture or the numbers. The bottom number is how many equal parts.",
"fz0u9k": "Tap a shape. Count its sides and corners.",
"ibs7u1": "Read the clock and the ruler. Move the sliders!",
"18i04x3": "Read the bars. Move the sliders!",
"1x34oq0": "Read the story. Find the key words. Then pick the math.",
"g47ftg": "Addition means putting two amounts together. Line up the digits and add column by column. When a column adds up to 10 or more, carry 1 to the next column on the left.",
"1l41u21": "Try once more. Add the ones first, then the next column. Remember to carry.",
"bi0wco": "Subtraction means taking some away from the amount you started with. When the top digit is smaller than the bottom digit, borrow 10 from the next column on the left.",
"1liyldi": "Try once more. Subtract the ones first. Borrow if the top digit is too small. Check with addition.",
"1pjazdf": "Multiplication is repeated addition made shorter. Pick a square in the table to see the dots.",
"1qlxkdg": "Division means sharing equally. Move the sliders to share marbles into bags.",
"vv0zrb": "A fraction shows part of a whole that is split into equal parts. Change the denominator and the numerator, then look at the picture.",
"4rm6e6": "Perimeter is the distance around a shape. Area is the space inside. Move the sliders and watch both change. Then try angles.",
"p2mwe4": "Try once more. Draw the shape if you can. Remember the formula and write the units.",
"1o0j81i": "Units help us measure. Big units and small units are linked. Change the number to see how. Then find out when something ends.",
"1w5rxbi": "Try once more. Check the units first. Change to the same unit before you calculate.",
"jx5b5h": "Bar charts can count in 2s. Tally marks count votes: each group of 5 has a line through it.",
"1xs643b": "Word problems turn everyday stories into math. Follow these four steps.",
"6r7193": "To multiply big numbers, break one number into place-value parts, multiply each part, then add the answers. Type your own numbers below.",
"m1ndaz": "Try once more. Break a number into tens and ones, multiply each part, then add.",
"17uea5q": "Division means sharing equally or making equal groups. Type a number and a divisor to see the answer and what is left over.",
"y5tnsl": "A fraction shows part of a whole that is split into equal parts. Change the denominator and the numerator, then look at the picture. Fractions can be equal even when they look different.",
"8lsgh": "Perimeter is the distance around a shape. Area is the space inside it, counted in square units. Angles are measured in degrees.",
"oblket": "Change between units by multiplying or dividing by 10, 100 or 1,000. Then work out when an activity ends.",
"a3qb23": "Data helps us see what is common. The mode is the number that appears most. The range tells how spread out the numbers are.",
"hanmz0": "Try once more. Mode is the number that appears most often. Range is biggest minus smallest.",
"11gqaql": "A fraction can also be a decimal or a percent. Change the denominator and the numerator and watch all three forms.",
"si99ma": "The area of a triangle is half of a rectangle. Volume is how much space a box fills, counted in cubic units. Try each tool.",
"1o2oa9j": "Speed tells how far something goes in one hour. Try the calculators, and change units too.",
"1xtrakl": "The mean is the average. The median is the middle number when the numbers are in order. Move the sliders and see.",
"53zklx": "Try once more. Mean is the total divided by how many. Median is the middle number in order.",
"mixh7f": "A circle has a radius and a circumference. We use π ≈ 3.14. Try each tool.",
"1e88ltj": "Speed, time and distance are linked. Maps use a scale, and ratios help us scale up recipes. Try each tool.",
"1hn5y0d": "Mean, median, mode and range describe a set of numbers. Change the six numbers and watch.",
